anted it now whereas this is going up  in it's mine you know exactly when you  own property  you take care to preserve it to allow it  to keep producing good things but we  pilgrims shared our lands so when the  crops were ready to harvest we did what  these people did some of my neighbors  sneaked out at night and grabbed extra  food some picked corn before it was  fully ready the result by the spring our  food stores what are you was it not the  shortage of food was worse because of a  second problem with the Commons when you  share the results of your work some  people don't work hard for it let an  opportunity for some to take advantage  and leave the work to others have that  continued Thursday would be known as  starvation day but fortunately we were  led not by Bernie Sanders or other  Commons loving socialists but by  Governor William Bradford who wrote in  his diary after much debate ie William  Bradford assign it to every family a  parcel of land he did what I did here  the result this had very good success  for it made all hands very industrious  we brought in a harvest that was more  than enough to feed us after such a  success we never returned to shared  planting private property allowed us  pilgrims to prosper and have that feast  we read about at school so this  Thanksgiving if you have a good meal  think private property every day it  protects us from the tragedy of the  Commons  you
 

